r, a long-acting, acylated analog of human insulin</article-title><source>Pharm Res</source><year>2004</year><volume>21</volume><fpage>1498</fpage><lpage>1504</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15359587</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b9-vhrm-5-121"><label>9.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Philips</surname><given-names>JC</given-names></name><name><surname>Scheen</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Insulin detemir in the treatment of type 1 and type 2 diabetes</article-title><source>Vasc Health Risk Manag</source><year>2006</year><volume>2</volume><fpage>277</fpage><lpage>283</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17326333</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b10-vhrm-5-121"><label>10.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Heise</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Nosek</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>R&#x000f8;nn</surname><given-names>BB</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Lower within-subject variability of insulin detemir in comparison to NPH insulin and insulin glargine in people with type 1 diabetes</article-title><source>Diabetes</source><year>2004</year><volume>53</volume><fpage>1614</fpage><lpage>1620</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15161770</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b11-vhrm-5-121"><label>11.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Rosenstock</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Dailey</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Massi-Benedetti</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Reduced Hypoglycemia Risk With Insulin Glargine: A meta-analysis comparing insulin glargine with human NPH insulin in type 2 diabetes</article-title><source>Diabetes Care</source><year>2005</year><volume>28</volu